{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_libuv_thread_pool", "label": "The libuv thread pool", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_four_spare_threads", "label": "Four spare threads to block on your behalf", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Portable filesystem calls block, so libuv hands the call to a worker thread and posts the result back. Network I/O uses no threads."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_uv_threadpool_size", "label": "UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Default 4, max 1024. Created lazily on first use; size is fixed from then on. Set it in the environment before the process starts."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_dns_lookup_uses_pool", "label": "dns.lookup uses the thread pool", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every outbound fetch, http.request and database connection resolves through dns.lookup by default, so a burst of HTTP can make unrelated fs reads slow."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_dns_resolve_no_pool", "label": "dns.resolve does not use the thread pool", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "resolve4 talks to a DNS server directly and ignores /etc/hosts. The usual fix for pool pressure is a DNS cache in front of lookup, not swapping to resolve."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_worker_threads_vs_pool", "label": "Thread pool versus worker_threads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The pool is internal and runs C/C++ only. worker_threads each run their own V8 isolate and JavaScript."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_libuv_thread_pool", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_four_spare_threads", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_libuv_thread_pool", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_uv_threadpool_size", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_libuv_thread_pool", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_0_runtime_model_04_libuv_thread_pool_dns_lookup_uses_pool", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-0-runtime-model/04-libuv-thread-pool.md", "source_location": null, "weig